I hate you this time.

140
00:07:37,760 --> 00:07:38,780
Yeah, yeah, I know.

141
00:07:42,200 --> 00:07:43,080
It's good.

142
00:07:43,380 --> 00:07:44,820
Oh, I'm glad you like it.

143
00:07:44,820 --> 00:07:45,820
Oh?

144
00:07:47,220 --> 00:07:47,780
Hmm.

145
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:50,320
Here.

146
00:07:51,340 --> 00:07:52,840
This way we'll be even.

147
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:56,080
Why are you hesitating?

148
00:07:56,440 --> 00:07:57,720
Go ahead, take a bite.

149
00:08:02,900 --> 00:08:05,220
You know, that's almost like we kissed.

150
00:08:05,220 --> 00:08:12,080
Shiori, look, over here.

151
00:08:12,620 --> 00:08:13,680
It's a ring toss.

152
00:08:13,880 --> 00:08:15,040
These are so much fun.

153
00:08:15,760 --> 00:08:17,140
So which prize do you want?

154
00:08:17,440 --> 00:08:19,260
You just name it and I'll get it for you.

155
00:08:19,420 --> 00:08:22,460
Uh, uh, the cat, I guess.

156
00:08:23,340 --> 00:08:23,800
Okay.

157
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:26,640
Watch, I'll get it on the first try.

158
00:08:29,220 --> 00:08:30,000
Take that!

159
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,700
Oh, man.

160
00:08:32,240 --> 00:08:33,880
That's way harder than I thought.

161
00:08:34,920 --> 00:08:36,300
What are you, a clown?

162
00:08:36,540 --> 00:08:38,460
Stop laughing and win the prize, dummy!

163
00:08:38,500 --> 00:08:38,760
Right.

164
00:08:39,540 --> 00:08:41,740
Hey, Miku, why don't you let me try?

165
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:44,420
You are going to give me that touch the cat at once.

166
00:08:45,700 --> 00:08:46,500
Of course!

167
00:08:47,340 --> 00:08:48,620
Here, it's all yours!

168
00:08:48,620 --> 00:08:52,760
Here you are, Shiori.

169
00:08:54,080 --> 00:08:55,720
Why did you do that, Miku?

170
00:08:55,860 --> 00:08:56,440
It's wrong.

171
00:08:56,460 --> 00:08:56,760
Shino!

172
00:08:57,160 --> 00:08:58,840
Oh, is this not the one you wanted?

173
00:08:59,240 --> 00:09:00,580
Because I'm happy to exchange it for you.

174
00:09:00,580 --> 00:09:00,960
That's not it!

175
00:09:01,580 --> 00:09:02,700
What's wrong with you?

176
00:09:02,820 --> 00:09:04,080
That's not how things work!

177
00:09:04,180 --> 00:09:07,580
Oh, well, in that case, what am I supposed to do?

178
00:09:07,660 --> 00:09:10,580
If you won a prize, you win the game fair and square, okay?

179
00:09:10,820 --> 00:09:11,220
Okay.

180
00:09:11,920 --> 00:09:14,300
But what happens if I lose and still want the prize?

181
00:09:14,320 --> 00:09:15,740
You give up or keep trying.

182
00:09:16,140 --> 00:09:17,760
Just think about the people who work here.

183
00:09:18,080 --> 00:09:20,480
Don't you think it would make them sad to know they've been manipulated?

184
00:09:21,440 --> 00:09:21,880
Sad?

185
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:26,900
They should be over the moon that I would even accept a stupid prize from their silly cultural festival.

186
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:27,860
You're kidding, right?

187
00:09:28,180 --> 00:09:29,860
Listen, don't worry about them.

188
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:31,560
They're my playthings, nothing more.

189
00:09:31,560 --> 00:09:34,800
They're my dumb little pawns, and I use them to get whatever I want.

190
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:37,400
You should know I think very highly of you, though.

191
00:09:37,580 --> 00:09:39,540
So it's not something you need to worry about.

192
00:09:39,540 --> 00:09:41,440
How incredibly sad.

193
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:42,620
